v 3
d csdid: Callaway-Sant'Anna group-time average treatment effects
d
d A Mata implementation of group-time average treatment effects, with doubly
d robust, regression and IPW estimators and multiplier-bootstrap inference.
d
d csdid estimates group-time average treatment effects ATT(g,t) for
d difference-in-differences designs with staggered treatment timing, following
d Callaway and Sant'Anna (2021, Journal of Econometrics), with doubly robust,
d outcome-regression and inverse-probability-weighted estimators from
d Sant'Anna and Zhao (2020, Journal of Econometrics).
d
d Aggregation (simple, dynamic/event study, group and calendar), analytical and
d multiplier-bootstrap inference with simultaneous confidence bands, and
d postestimation export and plotting are provided by csdid_stats, csdid_estat
d and csdid_plot.
d
d Unlike the SSC csdid, this implementation does not require drdid: the
d doubly robust, outcome-regression and IPW estimators are implemented
d internally, so the package has no dependencies.
d
d On macOS the multiplier bootstrap uses a compiled accelerator plugin
d (universal binary, Intel and Apple silicon). On other platforms, or if
d the plugin cannot load, csdid falls back to the Mata implementation
d automatically; results are identical either way.
d
d KW: difference in differences
d KW: DID
d KW: difference-in-differences
d KW: event studies
d KW: staggered treatment adoption
d KW: treatment effects
d KW: causal inference
